# Tests: extend existing cases

When changing or adding a feature, cover it with tests — but read the existing suite first.

Prefer **new assertions on an existing test** that already exercises the same unit, fixture, or flow. Add a new test file or function only when no current case is a natural home (different setup, different entrypoint, or a regression that would make an existing test unreadable).

```python
# ❌ BAD — extra test that only exists for one new field
def test_generate_omits_prompt_graph():
    puzzles = generate(...)
    assert "prompt_graph" not in puzzles[0]

# ✅ GOOD — same check on the pipeline/CLI test that already builds puzzles
def test_refresh_fixtures_generate_validate_inspect(...):
    ...
    for p in puzzles:
        assert "prompt_graph" not in p
        assert p["quality_score"] >= 3  # new behavior
```

Same idea in Go and frontend tests: fold the new expectation into `TestSolve`, `test_help`, etc., rather than a one-off `TestXDoesYWhenZ`.
